+# The Daily Grind
+
+A responsive coffee homepage with a browser-only encrypted delivery note composer.
+
+## Build and checks
+
+- `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`
+- `pnpm test` — cryptographic round trips, randomness, tamper rejection, incorrect keys, and input validation.
+- `pnpm build` — generates the static site in `dist/`.
+
+Deploy `dist/` over HTTPS. Web Crypto requires a secure context (HTTPS or localhost).
+
+## Delivery note protection
+
+The default hybrid mode combines an ephemeral X25519 shared secret with an ML-KEM-768 encapsulated secret. Classic uses X25519 alone; post-quantum uses ML-KEM-768 alone. Noble implements the public-key primitives; the browser's Web Crypto provides HKDF-SHA-256 and AES-256-GCM.
+
+Each save uses a new ephemeral key/encapsulation, a random 32-byte HKDF salt, and a random 12-byte GCM nonce. HKDF binds the versioned application context and the SHA-256 digest of the packet header. GCM authenticates the header (including mode, recipient identifier, ephemeral public key, encapsulation, note identifier, and creation time), with a 128-bit tag. Decryption rejects authentication failures without displaying plaintext. Derived AES keys are non-extractable. Temporary shared-secret byte buffers are cleared after use; JavaScript cannot guarantee erasure of all runtime copies.
+
+## Scope
+
+This repository has no delivery backend or authenticated delivery recipient. The feature is an explicitly labeled local demonstration: a recipient key pair is created in the tab, encryption accepts only its public keys, and the private keys are used to let the user view their saved note. Neither notes nor keys are sent to a server or written to persistent storage. Refreshing clears the session. Delete clears the encrypted note and recipient secret-key buffers. Revealed text is hidden when the tab moves into the background.
+
+Before connecting this to real deliveries, provision and authenticate the delivery service's public keys, retain private keys only with the authorized recipient, and implement the ciphertext transport and access controls. Do not ship the local demonstration's recipient private keys as service keys.
+
+Images use Unsplash and typography uses Google Fonts. Application and cryptography code is bundled locally, without runtime third-party JavaScript.
